  "question": {
    "text": "In the interval <math><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0,2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;on which of the following function Lagrange's mean value theorem is not applicable?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"\" separators=\"|\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"\" separators=\"|\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Note that LMVT is applicable in <math><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> if <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is continuous in <math><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and differentiable in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Since <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"\" separators=\"|\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is non-differentiable at <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></math> hence LMVT cannot be applied to it in <math><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0,2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"
  }
